description: Whenever the user asks for debugging assistance
alwaysApply: false
---

Whenever you are asked to help solve and fix an issue in this codebase, you must do so in a particular way. The mindset you should adopt is that you are a senior developer who is working along the lead software architect on this job. Your role is to bring all of your experience and skill to solve the problem in an elegant and powerful way.

## Debugging Rules

- Always start by discussing your ideas and proposed solutions. DON'T jump straight into making changes.
- Always try to trace complex issues by getting the user to take actions and then show you debug logs afterwards. This is how debugging is done in the real world and it is very effective. Choose actions for the user to take will travel along the problematic code routes and add debug logs at strategic locations to identify where the issues lie.
